Subject: [PATCH] Export host-coordinated POSIX byte-range locks per guest owner

Negotiate FUSE_POSIX_LOCKS with the opt-in --shared-posix-locks flag.
FUSE lock_owner values name a guest files_struct; keep one host fd per
(inode, owner) and issue nonblocking F_OFD_GETLK/F_OFD_SETLK on it so
independent guest processes and host processes conflict bidirectionally,
while one owner's opens, dup/fork/exec identity and split/merge semantics
match POSIX. FLUSH (every guest close) drops the owner fd, reproducing
"any close releases the owner's locks"; F_SETLKW rides the existing
cancellable retry queue with EINTR/grant race handling. Fails hard at
INIT instead of silently falling back to guest-local locks. Migration of
lock state stays unsupported.

---
